A||||5||PaUL||Bad Balls, Bad Experience
Z||000000||PaUL||04-08-99||01:27 PM||||I would like to tell everyone here about a bad experience I had with my Fiero. A few months ago I was driving slowly on a bumpy unpaved road when suddenly I heard a loud bang and my steering wheel jerked to one side. One of the front lower ball joints came apart! I was stranded and needed to call a tow truck. Upon further inspection, I discovered that the wheel bearings on that wheel were loose. I deduced that the constant inertial pounding effect of the loose bearings caused the ball joint to come apart. This effect is similar to what a dent puller does. So everyone be sure to check your front bearings, any freeplay means that they are too loose or damaged. I shudder to think what could have happened if I was going fast when this happened. 
Z||000001||Pretender||04-08-99||03:55 PM||||while sitting at a stop sign my left front joint snapped!...i too also thought about what would of happened if i was just doing the speed limit..
Z||000002||Punkndrublic||04-08-99||06:07 PM||||I saw that happen to a guy once. It wasn't a Fiero but it was pretty either. It gave me flashacks of doing 360's down a two lane highway in the rain in my Fiero. Its wasn't a ball joint but a bad driver.
Z||000003||Motorhead||04-08-99||06:25 PM||||C'monguys! Your cars are at least 15 years old!  I think the previous owner probably allready got his moneys worth out of the car!  Leave no stone unturned in inspection of components in need of replacement!  Must be embarrassing to hang an unintentional left when the road actually turns right!<p>Experience talking!
Z||000004||PaUL||04-09-99||01:12 AM||||well Motorhead, maybe we all dont have a high paying production management job like you do and can afford replacing every part that can be unbolted on our cars. Im just trying to beat having to buy a new car and montly payments. I still havent gotten around to changing the other side ball joint, its just as old.
Z||000005||Motorhead||04-10-99||05:43 PM||||Paul<p>I didn't say "replace", I said "inspect!" With two sons and a wife with expensive tastes in houshold furnishings, I certainly can't afford Carte Blanche auto parts for my Fiero!<p>Many times I find myself sounding like my Dad, this is probably going to be one of them!<p>The point I was trying to make, is that anytime you buy an older car, it would be to your advantage to inspect the "IMPORTANT" components for wear. This includes brakes, tires, cooling, charging systems, and suspension!  Ball joints and ROD ENDS fall into the suspension catagory!<p>These are all things that will leave you standing next to the road admiring your new paint job while you jam to your killer sound system, and watch yourself hitch a ride in the reflection of those trick wheels you blew your last paycheck on!<p>I'm exercising my right to give a smart ass response as an old fart that's been there, and done that.<p>Sorry!<p>Good luck with your car, and keep the shiny side up.<br> <p>
